<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n108957" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπόπλᾰτυς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">υ,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>somewhat extended,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν τοῖσι στήθεσι ἐρυθήματα ὑ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Coac.</u>
					410
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>rather flat,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπέρμα [ἀλύσσου</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				3.91
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σχῆμα ὑ. ὁμοίως τοῖς φακοῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					6.551
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>somewhat salt, brackish,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Dicaearch.
				1.27
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
